WEBVTT

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:18.890
Go, Miyano!

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.770
Good job, Miyano.

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:30.980
Thanks.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:34.860
Well done.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.410
Kuresawa.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:40.200
Thanks.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.830
It's so hot today.

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:45.000
Miyano, you're pretty fast,
despite being an indoor kid.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.670
I'd like to be indoors. I'm so thirsty.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.460
Want me to get you something?
You can pay me later.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.260
I'm gonna grab some juice.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.130
A sports drink, then.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:57.140
You got it. You gonna stay here?

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.430
No, I'm gonna wash my face.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:01.430
Okay, I'll find you later.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:03.100
Okay, thanks.

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:17.320
Why not grow your bangs?

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.620
You'll supposedly look older.
And maybe less feminine-faced.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.200
That's an idea.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:30.710
I grew my bangs out, but of course
now they're in the way...

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:31.840
Mya-<i>chan</i>?

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.760
Oh, it is you, Mya-<i>chan</i>.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:39.510
Sasaki-<i>senpai</i>.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.930
Are you taking refuge here, too?

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:43.770
Huh?

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.770
It's hot today, right?

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:48.350
There's a nice breeze here.

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.770
Is your event over?

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.520
Yes. I just finished mine.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.940
Then let's shoot the breeze.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.360
Skipping out early?

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.200
No, it's just a break.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:21.510
"Sasaki and Miyano"

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.170
"Episode 5: 'Bit by Bit'"

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.090
"Episode 5: 'Bit by Bit'"
What was your event?

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:37.420
"Episode 5: 'Bit by Bit'"
The 1,500-meter run.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.510
Are you a strong runner?

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:44.340
Not at short-distance, but I guess
I'm fairly good at long-distance.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.890
Oh, wow. Impressive.

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:52.940
Are you on the white team? Me, too.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.270
Thank you.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:57.440
Huh?

00:03:57.900 --> 00:03:59.650
"Delayed embarrassment"

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.860
What was yours, Senpai?

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:06.950
Basket toss. It's basically
compulsory for tall people.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.490
I can see that.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.700
Hirano would have had to play, too,

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:15.670
but as a freshman he caused trouble
and was banned from basket toss.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:17.250
Hirano-<i>senpai </i>did?!

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:19.670
What did he do?

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.840
"Gimme your jacket! I'm making a pouch!"

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:21.840
He yanked his classmates' PE clothes off,

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:26.930
"Hey, I'm cold!"
"Gimme your jacket! I'm making a pouch!"

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:26.930
He yanked his classmates' PE clothes off,

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:25.340
"Hey, I'm cold!"
"Gimme your jacket! I'm making a pouch!"

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:25.340
filled them with balls,
and tossed them in.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.260
"Hey, I'm cold!"
"Gimme your jacket! I'm making a pouch!"

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.260
Hirano-<i>senpai</i>...

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:31.350
The other classes started
copying him and things got crazy.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:33.730
It wasn't basket toss anymore.

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:35.480
--Clothes were scattered everywhere,
and some people tried to get naked...

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.060
--Thank goodness.
--Clothes were scattered everywhere,
and some people tried to get naked...

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:39.980
I'm talking pretty normally with him.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.400
"Thank goodness?"

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.070
--So I read that manga...

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.610
--Why did I think tha--
--So I read that manga...

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.360
O-Oh? Yes?

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:50.700
You know, there was this part
where they kiss through a mask.

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.330
It was kinda nice.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:55.750
When stuff like that happens,
it's... delightful?

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:00.920
I like talking with him.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:03.210
That's... yeah...

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.300
How do I describe it?

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.300
--I'm reading alone, but I get excited...

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:13.020
--I never imagined we'd
talk about my hobby.
--I'm reading alone, but I get excited...

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:16.850
But whether that "like"
is love, I'm not sure.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:17.850
Oh,

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.320
is this what <i>moe </i>is?

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.360
Yes!

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.360
Yes. Yes it is!

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.360
Senpai, you get it.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:27.110
That's a standard plotline.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:33.580
--Actually, maybe I just
misheard him on the train.
--But the classics are classic for a reason!

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:37.250
It's not like he's said
anything directly since then.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.830
So maybe...

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:42.840
Huh, I feel like maybe
my spirits have been lifted.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.800
--You can see why it's a classic!
--Yeah.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:49.390
I also like how the kisser
gets sick despite the mask,

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:52.470
and they take turns
taking care of each other!

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:55.230
He's so cute.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.520
The <i>uke </i>tries and fails to make soup.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:00.360
I feel like the <i>ukes</i>
are often bad at cooking.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:04.730
That might just be a coincidence
in the manga I tend to buy.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.570
--I enjoy talking with him.
--Oh, it is?

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:09.160
I also like it when the <i>seme </i>can't cook,

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:12.490
--I enjoy being with him.
--but the authors I usually buy
tend not to go that route.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.040
"Let's win our last Field Day!"

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:14.040
Oh, I see.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.830
"Let's win our last Field Day!"

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.830
--When I like a particular couple,
I buy all their stuff...

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:21.170
"Let's win our last Field Day!"

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:21.170
--When I like a particular couple,
I buy all their stuff...
--I want this to go on forever.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:25.880
I don't want it to end after I graduate.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.930
Hey, Mya-<i>chan</i>.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:33.220
Yes?

00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:36.270
I like you, Miyano.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.030
What?

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.160
What I said in the summer...

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:03.130
I'm not taking that back.

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:17.020
--I--
--Miyano?

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:23.520
Um...

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:29.440
Um, I, uh...

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:37.290
Does this wavering mean there's a chance?

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:42.210
I can wait...

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:44.830
You don't have to answer right away.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:48.090
I'd be happy if you gave it some thought.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:50.800
I will!

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:52.180
I swear!

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:57.810
Great.

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:01.640
Kuresawa is calling for you.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.850
Oh...

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.310
...right.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:07.360
See ya later, Mya-<i>chan</i>.

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:24.120
I got nervous!

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.500
Sasaki-<i>senpai</i>.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.920
Can I ask you something?

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.300
S-Sure. What is it?

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:35.800
Sasaki-<i>senpai</i>,

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:38.600
what do you like about me?

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:43.310
Wh-What... do... I...?

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.730
Y-Your face...

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.740
O-Oh...

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:53.780
I'd better go now.

00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:55.450
My-Mya-<i>chan</i>!

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.070
I messed up!

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.330
There you are. Were you with Senpai?

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:01.870
U-Uh, yeah...

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.000
Senpai, did you say someth--

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.500
I'll tell you what it is next time.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.760
Here. Your tab is 140 yen.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.130
Thanks.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.180
The game of chicken is up next.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:29.650
I mean, I'm really into your face,

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:31.730
but that's not...

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:35.280
It's not just that...

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:37.280
Your eyes...

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:41.830
The excited way you talk to me...

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:45.080
The way you look right at me...

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:49.460
You remember what I say...

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:51.590
And on White Day...

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:56.260
What you've done for me...

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:59.510
All of it...

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:03.260
I like all of it.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:05.430
And yet I...

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:07.770
Ugh, dammit!

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:10.020
I got caught off guard.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:15.440
Expressing feelings is hard.

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:20.240
...asaki!

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:21.740
Sasaki!

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:23.740
Sasaki!

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:25.290
Huh?

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:27.370
That's quite the getup.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:31.920
I was part of the cheer squad.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:34.750
The class relay is up next.

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:36.130
Right...

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:39.800
What's wrong?

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:44.430
You know, I just passed by Miyano.

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:46.600
My-Mya-<i>chan</i>?

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:50.400
Seriously, what's wrong?

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:54.570
Do you feel sick?
Want me to sub in for you?

00:10:54.570 --> 00:11:01.490
The other day I borrowed a manga
about time slips from Miyano.

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:04.740
If this is about a BL manga, I'm out.

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:08.080
I get enough of that from Miyano.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.500
BL...

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.920
BL, huh...

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:14.540
Is it BL?

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.550
What do you think, Hirano?

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:19.340
What are you talking about?

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:21.890
If you can race, then hurry up.

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:23.850
Everyone's waiting.

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:25.600
I'm going.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:36.520
I wanna be cool.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:47.870
At first it didn't bother me.

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:50.000
Miyano has such a cute face.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.790
Like he makes a better girl than a girl.

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:57.590
But it happened over and over again...

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:01.470
I got sick of it,

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:03.800
and I steadily grew more insecure.

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:19.230
Is it because I have a cold?

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:21.240
What an awful dream.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:24.070
My face...

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:33.830
What does he mean when he calls me cute?

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:37.170
Is it because of my feminine face?

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:39.670
I don't want to be a girl.

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:44.510
I would've preferred a manlier face.

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:47.260
If only I were a few inches taller...

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:50.100
Then I could have more confidence,

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:52.310
and I could give Senpai...

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:02.440
What am I even thinking?

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:04.530
What does he mean he likes my face?

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:08.410
Ah, I'm going in circles!

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.000
It's endless.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:21.630
How do I feel about Sasaki-<i>senpai</i>?

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:28.640
With the long break and exams
coming up, the Discipline Committee

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:33.350
will be conducting morning dress code
checks before the exam period.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:36.020
Any questions so far?

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:41.900
Yes. What if a Committee member
is violating the dress code?

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:42.980
Like who?

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:46.650
"Dress Code Checks"

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:46.650
A certain blond individual.

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:47.860
"Dress Code Checks"

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:47.860
Oh, me.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:48.370
"Blind Spot"

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:49.950
"Dress Code Checks"

00:13:48.370 --> 00:13:49.950
--I'm heading out!
--A written apology gets you
an exemption for dyed hair.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:50.870
"Dress Code Checks"

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:50.870
--Thanks for coming.
--A written apology gets you
an exemption for dyed hair.

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:53.040
--Thanks for coming.
--A written apology gets you
an exemption for dyed hair.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.660
That's not an exemption...

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:58.750
It'd be a pain to dye it
back for every test.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:01.630
You dyed it back for the closing ceremony.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:05.420
Well, I was also gonna see
some relatives over the break.

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:09.140
It'd destroy my hair
to do that every time.

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:12.220
I've always wondered...

00:14:12.220 --> 00:14:16.020
Hirano-<i>senpai</i>, why do you
dye your hair blond?

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:17.560
'Cause it's cool.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:19.480
Right. Of course.

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:21.860
Quit laughing, Chairman.

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:24.940
Once I used a spray
to make it black for a day.

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:29.740
But then my hair was all stiff
and wouldn't lay right. It was terrible.

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:32.950
Still, it costs money
to actually dye it back,

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:35.450
and it costs money to redye it, too.

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:37.620
Couldn't you just not dye it?

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:39.540
No way.

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:43.090
It sounds like a lot of work.

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:46.590
Sasaki told you he dyed
his hair black his first year, right?

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:47.590
Yes.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:52.600
At one point, once the color was
falling out, he looked like a calico cat.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:55.270
Sasaki-<i>senpai</i>...

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:56.890
...a calico cat?

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:01.980
Oh, when you're done,
help me with these printouts.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:03.020
Will do.

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:18.620
Now this is unusual.

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:21.710
I'll go hand over the duty chart.

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:23.080
Okay.

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:28.670
It must be hot wearing
a mask in the summer.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:36.930
--Hir--
--Shh!

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:38.390
...rano...

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:43.020
The teacher asked me to get you.

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:44.310
Got it.

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:47.150
He's sleeping.

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:49.150
Don't wake him up.

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:50.860
He doesn't feel well.

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:51.820
A cold?

00:15:51.820 --> 00:15:53.910
Probably.

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:59.040
If you have time,
could you stay until I come back?

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:00.660
Sure.

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:03.170
If he wakes up, tell him to go home.

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:04.580
Okay.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:47.960
If it's through a mask,

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:50.090
is it okay?

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:55.390
What did he call it? Standard?

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:00.930
Can I?

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:06.690
No, definitely not okay.

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:37.680
I'm hopeless.

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:42.850
I...

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:44.810
Oh, you were still sleeping?

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:46.390
Huh?

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:49.190
Sasaki-<i>senpai</i>!

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:50.610
Morning.

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:57.660
Good... morning...

00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:02.120
Miyano, if you're awake, go home.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:04.660
The term is almost over. Don't push it.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:05.620
Huh?

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:08.250
Um... is that okay?

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:10.500
Why not.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:12.960
Then I'll head home now.

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:14.130
See ya.

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:27.100
So?

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:30.860
Did you do something to Miyano?

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:33.530
He's acting strange.

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:40.530
I confessed my feelings.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:44.120
Excuse me?

00:18:44.120 --> 00:18:46.160
But I didn't say it right.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:49.750
I want to, but it feels like
he's avoiding me.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:52.840
Wait, "confessed?"

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:56.300
Should you be telling me?

00:18:58.300 --> 00:19:01.760
Um, do you not have Miyano's number?

00:19:01.760 --> 00:19:04.310
Huh? I don't, actually.

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:07.890
Why not?! After all that manga borrowing?

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:10.770
Look, it just sorta didn't...

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:11.860
Hey.

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:12.980
What is it?

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:16.570
Quit making excuses and just tell him.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:18.610
"Yoshikazu Miyano"

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.200
Thanks.

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:26.580
Yeah.

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:34.630
Are you guys leaving, too?
Let's go partway together!

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.130
Okay.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:37.050
"Hirano-<i>senpai</i>"

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.630
"Hirano-<i>senpai</i>"

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.630
Hirano-<i>senpai</i>?

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:41.180
"Hirano-<i>senpai</i>"

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:41.180
Did I forget something?

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:42.680
Yes?

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:44.220
Mya-<i>chan</i>?

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:49.480
Sasaki-<i>senpai</i>?

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:56.020
I really like that.

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:59.570
I want to hear him say that more.

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:05.490
I forgot to say something before.

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:07.660
So I borrowed Hirano's phone.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:11.210
Hey, listen...

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:13.000
Yes?

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:17.960
I like you a lot. For more than your face.

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:19.010
That's all.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:22.180
--Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh?
--See ya. And take care.

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:29.520
Sasaki, go let Miyano punch you.

00:20:29.520 --> 00:20:31.730
Actually, can<i> I </i>just punch you?

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:32.690
Uh-uh.

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:35.480
Your punch would hurt, so no way!

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:39.530
--I didn't--I didn't see this
BL sucker punch coming!

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:40.940
--Even your ears are red.
--I didn't--I didn't see this
BL sucker punch coming!

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:44.280
Shut up! Girlfriend-haver!

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:45.700
Wanna see a picture of her?

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:49.580
No. Once you get started,
you'll go for hours!

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:53.080
I don't think I've seen
your girlfriend. Show me!

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:54.670
Okay. Bow down while you look.

00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:55.880
Oop. Scary.

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:58.130
Hey, she's cute!

00:20:58.130 --> 00:20:59.630
Fall for her and you're dead.

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:02.510
Stop, Kuresawa. You're scaring me.

00:21:09.310 --> 00:21:12.060
Actually, though Miyano
has a feminine face,

00:21:12.060 --> 00:21:14.980
compared to a girl,
he's totally masculine.

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:17.980
That's right, Tashiro.
You're smart. Thanks.

00:21:17.980 --> 00:21:21.400
So I'm a genius like I thought?

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:24.820
He doesn't just like me
because of my face...

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:29.030
Why did I just feel relieved?!

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:31.080
What emotional range!

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:33.250
I'm amazed you know that term.

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:35.750
Because I'm smart?

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:37.540
Why're you laughing?!

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:41.340
Miyano said I'm smart!

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:43.630
--Relieved...
--Yup. You sure are.

00:21:43.630 --> 00:21:45.930
--Why?!
--I detect a tone!

00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:52.020
"Bit by Bit"

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:25.820
I told you to keep your hands off him.

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:27.570
I have.

00:23:27.570 --> 00:23:29.650
I think.

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:32.410
Is it serious?

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:33.830
Yeah.

00:23:35.370 --> 00:23:38.290
You know what? Nope. Forget all of this.

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:38.910
"Just don't do anything careless."

00:23:38.910 --> 00:23:41.330
"Just don't do anything careless."
This is creeping me out!

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:42.170
"I won't."

00:23:42.170 --> 00:23:45.000
"I won't."
Same.

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:47.460
"Episode 6: 'Feelings.'"
